WEBVTT

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.640
Oh, yeah?

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.130
I've got three girls.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.580
Am I lucky, or what?

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.570
Oh, yeah?

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:16.480
No probs. I'd lose if I did things by the book.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.540
I'm gonna totally blow Machiko away this year.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.500
It's about to start now. I'm just getting started.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.050
Miyu!

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.180
What took ya? You're gonna be late.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.600
Sorry!

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.650
Morning.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.960
Huh?

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.050
One has landed today.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.910
You can skip classes this morning, Miss Alien Fighter.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.360
It's been a long time since a spaceship landed.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.500
A week.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.210
I wish they'd stop landing here.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.050
If they did, I'd be bored... Bored to death.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.220
It's okay for you, you're doing this 'cause you want to.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.100
We'd better hurry, or Miss Hisagawa will get mad.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.450
Rock, scissors, paper!

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:28.810
That was scary.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.490
This spaceship...

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.830
Where did it come from?

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.290
Yuri!

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:53.750
Is there an alien there, or what, Yuri?

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:56.960
Nope, not in here.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.420
That's strange.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.500
It's not inside the spaceship.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.430
And there's no eyewitnesses.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.010
I wonder where it could have gone?

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.470
Is it possible that it left the school?

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.180
No.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.610
Well, let's keep looking for it, for the time being.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:15.820
Each of you patrol your areas thoroughly during the break.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.110
— All right?
— Okay.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.820
You've gotten pretty used to this, Yuri.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.160
You weren't scared, like that time.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.120
Yeah? Think so?

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.660
You'd better watch yourself.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.000
It's when you start getting used to the job that you make the most mistakes.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.640
I'm Hiroshi Iwanami, in the Camellia Class, Sixth Grade.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:43.590
My blood type is B, and my hobby is playing the trumpet.

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:55.810
Kumi said what she did, but I think I'm okay on my own now.

00:04:56.570 --> 00:05:00.860
I can learn to catch an alien on my own.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:14.710
If I can't find an alien, I'll have to stay at school.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.000
That's a drag.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:01.210
Yuri!

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:03.990
Yuri!

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:22.740
You're getting more and more depressed all the time.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.200
I think they're after me.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.280
"After you?"

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.620
Who is?

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:33.410
Aliens.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:36.700
I'm Manabu Namiki, in the Camellia Class, Sixth Grade.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.370
My blood type is B, and I like computers.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.560
Kumi! Kasumi!
Kumi! Kasumi!

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:27.610
I'm Tomoya Hironaka, in the Camellia Class, Sixth Grade.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:30.170
My blood type is B, and I like eating.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:15.840
Un, deux, trois, un, deux, trois...

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:17.510
Un!

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.580
Deux!

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:22.080
Trois!

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:39.780
Why...? Why are they only after me?

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:43.710
Pull yourself together!

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.380
You're always hiding behind other people!

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:50.780
Now there's only one alien at a time, but what would happen if there were lots?!

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:53.800
Anyway, there's nothing scary at all about these things!

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:02.170
Don't cry!

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:15.020
Miss Ootani!

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.530
Where've you been? Your Borg escaped, you know.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.200
Here, go and catch it.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.030
Uh, right.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:31.150
Good luck, Miss Ootani!

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:32.700
Unreal...

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.300
Okay, I'll try my best.

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:38.810
What a drag, right?

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:40.710
You can't stand it, right?

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:42.690
You can't do it, right?

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.620
This isn't funny, right?

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.230
Found you! Wait!

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:49.780
Wait!

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:54.480
Kumi...

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:04.160
Do it on your own.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:09.670
Help me, Kumi!

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.030
I always have these dreams.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:54.550
I wanna quit.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:11.100
— This way!
— Wait up!

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:14.480
Yuri!

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:17.710
It's Sunday. How come you're just sitting there?

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:19.840
Did you call your friends?

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:20.450
My friends?

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.480
What're you saying?

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:26.000
It's your birthday today.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.080
I forgot!

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:33.580
This is the worst! This is the worst year ever!

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:42.550
Kumi!

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:46.680
So you came, Kawamura. I called you.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.240
What? Oh...

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:51.100
Sorry.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.690
That wasn't very nice, coming on your own.

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:56.040
Oh well, the timing's perfect.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.650
Yuri'll be glad that we've all come at once.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:08.220
I knew it would be worrying you.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.560
It's not worrying me.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.620
I'm just wondering if maybe I said too much yesterday.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:17.600
So I was kinda worried.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:24.930
Kumi?

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:29.930
I'm going home.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:32.480
Hey, what're you doing, Kasumi?!

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.770
What is it, Kasumi?! Let me go!

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.150
What's your problem, Kasumi?

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:50.470
Alright, Kasumi. I won't go home.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.290
Hey, Yuri.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.970
Miyu. Kasumi.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.430
Kumi... Kawamura...!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.950
Uh...

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:11.990
H-Hap...

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:15.140
Happy... birthday.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.370
It's a good opportunity this year.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:38.060
Last year and the year before, no one would do it.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:40.680
But this year all of a sudden I've got two.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:43.920
If I play my cards right, I might even have three.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.720
You're lucky, Megu.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.260
I haven't had anyone in four years.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:51.300
That's the lousy part of being in charge of School No. 3.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:56.960
I have three, but one of them is a problem.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:01.800
Maybe you rushed things, using an attack alien.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.110
One order of fried chicken, please.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:20.310
I don't want Machiko in School No. 6 to beat me.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:23.340
I'll have to start getting tough with them tomorrow.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:24.730
Blow out the candles!

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.910
Okay!

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.770
Happy birthday!

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.540
I'm bored.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:12.600
Oh, I've got mail.

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:15.840
Out of stock?

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.180
Aw...

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:20.750
They told me they still had some left.

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.230
Give me a break.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:31.060
I can still use these though, so I guess it's okay.

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:06.520
I wish you'd stop looking at me and sighing every morning.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.360
I've got more things to be depressed about.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:14.320
Please don't forget about the reducing by the greatest common divisor...

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:17.510
...that we've been doing recently.

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:21.200
And one other thing to be careful with.

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:23.580
I'll give you a hint: The parentheses.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.580
Now, please get started.

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:29.000
Why're they looking at me?

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:33.320
Ever since the aliens got them, those three guys have been acting weird.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.630
I can't take it!

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.010
Note for you.

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:45.270
Miss Popular, let's go shopping after school.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.200
Hang in there. From Miyu.

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:37.450
Aren't you guys bored these days, no matter what you do?

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.410
Yeah, that's it.

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:44.160
Nothing's been fun since the time we put the aliens on.

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:46.750
Nope, nothing.

00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:55.340
This is the best.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:18:02.310
From now on, we're going to let Miss Ootani feed the aliens on her own.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:04.900
Huh?

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:08.520
I think it's too tough for her on her own.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.320
She'll be fine.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:13.280
She's the oldest after all.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:14.530
Right?

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:22.490
There's another thing to be depressed about.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:29.370
Oh.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:32.990
Yeah, so don't wait around for me.

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:34.460
I'll wait.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:37.800
We made plans to go shopping, right?

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.180
So hurry up and do your stuff.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:42.640
Thanks.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.950
This is alien hell.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.210
What year was the Alien Counter-Measure Party established?

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.170
2002. First in California.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.130
And the first contact?

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:20.620
October, 1998.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:21.760
Bingo!

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.600
Oh, are you two still here?

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:28.600
I'll stay on, so you two can go home.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.670
No, we'll wait until Yuri's done.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:32.560
Right.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:35.440
When was an alien being first discovered in Mars?

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.070
September, 2008.

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:39.240
Right! Perfect!

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:42.530
You're gonna get a perfect mark on the socials test!

00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:56.710
Why do I have to do this on my own...?

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:06.720
It would've been much faster if all three of us were feeding them.

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:14.780
Now, I just have the aliens in the water tanks left.

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:16.480
Wonder if Miyu will wait for me.

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:51.680
<i>Miss Popular, let's go shopping after school.</i>

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:52.480
<i>Hang in there.</i>

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:59.570
<i>From now on, we're going to let Miss Ootani feed the aliens on her own.</i>

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.530
I knew it...

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:15.000
I can't do this job.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:22.130
If we buy this and head to the beach, maybe Yuri will cheer up.

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:34.640
I'm scared... I'm so scared!

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:38.190
Yuri...!

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:45.570
I'm scared... I'm scared!
I'm scared... I'm scared!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.830
<i>You mustn't be that way, Miss Ootani.
You mustn't be afraid.</i>

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:54.010
<i>You mustn't run away.</i>

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:58.310
<i>Be brave. Overcome your fears.</i>

00:21:58.310 --> 00:21:59.670
<i>If you do that, then you can...</i>

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:10.340
I'm scared... I'm scared!
I'm scared... I'm scared!

00:22:10.340 --> 00:22:14.140
Somebody help!

00:23:57.510 --> 00:23:58.540
This is the worst.

00:24:01.480 --> 00:24:03.100
Don't worry.

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:04.670
It'll be fine.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:05.960
Don't cry, Kasumi.

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:46.280
Yuri...

00:24:48.300 --> 00:24:50.420
The Borgs...

00:25:03.140 --> 00:25:04.620
Yuri...?

00:25:07.750 --> 00:25:08.860
What happened to you?

00:25:13.890 --> 00:25:16.640
Miyu!

00:25:36.280 --> 00:25:37.430
Yuri...

00:25:42.810 --> 00:25:44.410
Yuri.

00:25:48.260 --> 00:25:51.320
See? I told you that you were pushing it.

00:25:51.610 --> 00:25:54.710
Come on, whose side are you on here?

00:25:54.710 --> 00:25:58.660
I might not sound like it, but I'm depressed.

00:25:59.500 --> 00:26:03.720
The board takes this very seriously.

00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:07.620
You might even be replaced by someone else.

00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:09.380
What?! Are you serious?!

00:26:10.640 --> 00:26:11.420
Yup.

00:26:11.420 --> 00:26:15.420
The End

00:28:04.810 --> 00:28:07.660
Kasumi...!

00:28:09.740 --> 00:28:10.660
Yuri...!

00:28:14.610 --> 00:28:16.820
Mum...!

00:28:18.170 --> 00:28:25.680
I'm scared!

00:28:26.690 --> 00:28:26.980
The End of
Summer Vacation
Borg
Death

00:28:26.980 --> 00:28:29.910
Dad!
